error[V0215]: `Task` cannot be written as a type
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0215_task_written_as_type/main.vr:6:15
  |
6 |     let task: Task<i64> = fetch(1);
  |               ^^^^^^^^^ `Task` cannot be written as a type
  |
  = note: a task's type is always worked out from the call that starts it, as in `let t = fetch(1);`, and a task stays in the function that started it, so no parameter, field, or return type can hold one
